SUMMARY:Sketching Carnivorous Plants in the Garden
DESCRIPTION:with Stacy-Ann Searle\, Landscape Artist \nHave you ever wanted to capture the beauty of carnivorous plants in your sketches while exploring the great outdoors? This workshop at the North Carolina Botanical Garden will immerse you in the peaceful practice of sketching nature. This session will focus on observing and sketching the Carnivorous Plant collection in various stages of growth\, encouraging participants to capture their unique perspectives and interpretations. \nREGISTER HERE \n 
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/sketching-carnivorous-plants-in-the-garden/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Learn
